From 0ce4d5017b3782de8a41381fd25271aa0600b2ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Bruno=20Greg=C3=B3rio?= <accounts@bruno.pw>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:25:01 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] drivers: add egisqsee, for Egis sensors behind Qualcomm
 TrustZone

TrustZone owns the SPI bus of the Egis EC617 in the Sony Xperia 10 VI;
Egis' trusted application egisap64 captures, matches and stores the
templates. The driver reaches it through the Linux TEE subsystem's
QSEECom device, attaching to the TA that qsee-supplicant's loader keeps
loaded, and drives the sensor's power, reset and finger interrupt through
the kernel's egisfp misc device. Prints name a template on the TA by its
finger id.

The enroll, verify and remove flows follow the vendor's Android agent,
from which they were recovered for interoperability.
